-class VideoPixelRateBudget {
+// The pixel rate the running instances of one direction have claimed. A component claims its pixel
+// rate when it starts, keeps the claim up to date as the stream changes and gives it back when it
+// stops, so the device refuses an instance its real-time streams would overload, as the framework
+// expects of a codec that reports its resources. The claims are those of the process, as the
